From 3c8bfde41dd7ee941b7cb5abc5470425d1c81427 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 02:47:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/16] Today's food: water, the meals of the plan and how they
 were followed

Patients followed by a nutritionist get "Today's food" on the follow-up
card, the nutrition part of the web app's day: calories and macronutrients
logged against the goals of the plan with what is left, water with the
+200/+300/+500 ml buttons of the web app against the personal goal, and
the meals of the plan with their items. Each meal is answered once a day:
"Followed" writes the prescribed items to the food diary and marks the
meal, as the web app does, then reloads the totals; "Partly followed" and
"Didn't follow" only record the answer.

The data comes from the server's day view, whose plans and meals have
UUIDs and whose decimals arrive as numbers or strings.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VRSTuUkoebWWM2DLbPZAvR
